Subject: [PATCH 2/3] e1_smooth --split: --margins M,... counts the smooth
 configurations within each margin of E(X), by a k-best enumeration that
 splits each smooth-playable heaviest set on its own members (item 4 of
 fable2-report.md, Section 4); --max-x searches the hub sets for the largest
 X-term, a best-first branch and bound on E(X_in) + F(H - X_out) with E and F
 cached, branching on a contended hub (item 2), with --e-seconds a budget for
 each search for E; the X-term takes any X, from no incumbent where the
 optimum's smooth part does not peel without it, with signed sides

